# Weather Systems — 96 bpm, A minor, one minute. Automation from
# expressions and chaotic systems: nothing below is drawn by hand except
# the notes.
#
#   beats  0-32   SWARM  three arpeggios panned by three voices of one
#                        Kuramoto swarm. The coupling rises through the
#                        section past the point where the swarm locks: the
#                        voices start scattered across the field and end
#                        moving as one. The pad's cutoff rides the Lorenz
#                        attractor for the whole song.
#   beats 32-64   MAP    drums and an acid line. The line's cutoff is the
#                        logistic map, one value per sixteenth, its r
#                        stepping up with each chord: one value (r = 2.8),
#                        two alternating (3.2), a cycle of four (3.5), then
#                        chaos (3.9). The hats' accents are the map in its
#                        chaotic regime; the bass filter wanders on noise.
#   beats 64-96   FALL   a bell FM'd by a muted modulator, its index swung
#                        by a double pendulum and its place in the field
#                        hopping on the Henon map; the swarm comes apart
#                        again as the coupling falls, and the tempo eases
#                        off at the end.
#
# The maps step on the sixteenths a quarter of a sixteenth early, so each
# new value has glided in (20 ms) by the time its note sounds.

bpm 96
gate 0.92
tail 4

section SWARM 0..32
section MAP 32..64
section FALL 64..96

automate reverb_wet
0.22
automate reverb_decay
0.78
automate comp_in
1
automate comp_threshold
-15
automate bpm
96 R:80 {96 - 10 * smoothstep(0, 1, p)}:16

# --- the bed: a pad on the Lorenz attractor, a bass on smooth noise
track pad patch=aurora vel=0.5 gain=0.7 reverb_send=0.35
([A2 E3 G3 B3 C4]:8 [F2 C3 E3 A3]:8 [C3 E3 G3 B3]:8 [G2 D3 E3 B3]:8)x3
automate pad.cutoff
{1500 + 1000 * lorenz(t / 3)}
automate pad.release
1.6

track bass patch=sunbass vel=0.8 gain=0.8
>MAP (A1:1.5 A1:0.5 R:1 A1:1 E2:1 R:1 A1:2 | F1:1.5 F1:0.5 R:1 F1:1 C2:1 R:1 F1:2 | C2:1.5 C2:0.5 R:1 C2:1 G2:1 R:1 C2:2 | G1:1.5 G1:0.5 R:1 G1:1 D2:1 R:1 G1:2)x2
automate bass.cutoff
{650 + 350 * noise(b / 3, 11)}

# --- SWARM and FALL: three arpeggios, panned by three voices of one swarm
track arp1 patch=glintbell vel=0.55 gain=0.4 reverb_send=0.3
((A4:0.25 C5:0.25 E5:0.25 B4:0.25)x8 (A4:0.25 C5:0.25 F5:0.25 E5:0.25)x8 (G4:0.25 C5:0.25 E5:0.25 B4:0.25)x8 (G4:0.25 B4:0.25 D5:0.25 E5:0.25)x8)
>FALL ((A4:0.25 C5:0.25 E5:0.25 B4:0.25)x8 (A4:0.25 C5:0.25 F5:0.25 E5:0.25)x8 (G4:0.25 C5:0.25 E5:0.25 B4:0.25)x8 (G4:0.25 B4:0.25 D5:0.25 E5:0.25)x8)
track arp2 patch=mallet vel=0.55 gain=0.45 reverb_send=0.3
((E4:0.5 A4:0.5)x8 (C4:0.5 F4:0.5)x8 (E4:0.5 G4:0.5)x8 (D4:0.5 G4:0.5)x8)
>FALL ((E4:0.5 A4:0.5)x8 (C4:0.5 F4:0.5)x8 (E4:0.5 G4:0.5)x8 (D4:0.5 G4:0.5)x8)
track arp3 patch=musicbox vel=0.5 gain=0.35 reverb_send=0.35
((A5:0.75 E5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (A5:0.75 F5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (G5:0.75 E5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (G5:0.75 D5:0.75 B4:0.5)x4)
>FALL ((A5:0.75 E5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (A5:0.75 F5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (G5:0.75 E5:0.75 C5:0.5)x4 (G5:0.75 D5:0.75 B4:0.5)x4)
automate arp1.release
0.45
automate arp1.pan
{0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 1)}:32 0:2@smooth >FALL {0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * (1 - p), 1)}:32
automate arp2.pan
{0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 4)}:32 0:2@smooth >FALL {0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * (1 - p), 4)}:32
automate arp3.pan
{0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 7)}:32 0:2@smooth >FALL {0.85 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * (1 - p), 7)}:32

# --- MAP: drums, and an acid line on the logistic map's period doubling
track kick patch=hardkick vel=0.9 gain=0.95
>MAP (A1 A1 A1 A1)x8
track hats kit=909 len=0.25 gain=0.5
>MAP (CH CH OH CH)x32
automate hats.gain
0.5 >MAP {0.2 + 0.6 * logistic(s * 4 + 0.25, 3.9)}:32
track claps kit=hats len=1
>MAP (R CP R CP)x8
track line patch=acidline vel=0.75 gain=0.7 reverb_send=0.12
>MAP (A2:0.25 A2:0.25 A3:0.25 A2:0.25)x8 (F2:0.25 F2:0.25 F3:0.25 F2:0.25)x8 (C3:0.25 C3:0.25 C4:0.25 C3:0.25)x8 (G2:0.25 G2:0.25 G3:0.25 G2:0.25)x8
automate line.cutoff
400 >MAP {300 * 2 ^ (4 * logistic(s * 4 + 0.25, seq(s / 8, 2.8, 3.2, 3.5, 3.9)))}:32

# --- FALL: a bell FM'd by a muted modulator, swung by a double pendulum
track bellmod patch=deepsine gain=0
>FALL D7:6 C7:2 | A#6:4 G6:4 | A6:4 F6:2 D6:2 | C7:6 A6:2
track bell patch=deepsine vel=0.7 gain=0.9 fm_from=bellmod fm=0 reverb_send=0.3 echo_send=0.15
>FALL E5:6 D5:2 | C5:4 A4:4 | B4:4 G4:2 E4:2 | D5:6 B4:2
automate bell.fm
0 >FALL {1.8 + 1.5 * pendulum(s / 2, 1)}:30 0:2@smooth
automate bell.pan
0 >FALL {0.5 * henon(s * 2 + 0.25)}:32
